    "title": "Sentence skylines, timing and ARMS",
    "summary": "Mr H: Listen to your rhythm. If every sentence is twelve words starting with 'The', your paragraph flatlines. Cam: Build a city skyline: long flowing sentences for panorama, then a sudden short sen...",
    "startSec": 375.25,
    "endSec": 463.16,
    "durationSec": 87.91,
    "embedHref": "/lessons/sitcom-descriptive-writing.html?embed=1#rhythm",
    "chapterId": "rhythm",
    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 377.05,
        "who": "mrh",
        "text": "Mr H: Listen to your rhythm. If every sentence is twelve words starting with 'The', your paragraph flatlines."
      },
      {
        "t": 384.39,
        "who": "cam",
        "text": "Cam: Build a city skyline: long flowing sentences for panorama, then a sudden short sentence for impact!"
      },
      {
        "t": 390.67,
        "who": "nib",
        "text": "Nib: Five shapes — Some Lazy Cats Fear Mice: Short, List, Complex, Fronted adverbial, and Minor sentence."
      },
      {
        "t": 398.75,
        "who": "will",
        "text": "Will: Dickens opens Bleak House with a two-word minor sentence: 'Fog everywhere.' No main verb — the fog simply sits there."
      },
      {
        "t": 407.14,
        "who": "nib",
        "text": "Nib: Punctuation controls timing. A colon holds your breath before a reveal: 'There was only one sound: the drip of the tap.'"
      },
      {
        "t": 416.29,
        "who": "mrh",
        "text": "Mr H: A semicolon balances two linked sentences; a dash jolts: 'The sea was calm — too calm.'"
      },
      {
        "t": 423.23,
        "who": "kevin",
        "text": "Kevin: Never stick me between two full sentences! 'The rain stopped, the steam rose' is a comma splice! Put me after a fronted adverbial: 'Beneath the awning, steam rose!'"
      },
      {
        "t": 433.26,
        "who": "mrh",
        "text": "Mr H: Finally, plan your picture in three layers — background, midground, foreground — and redraft with ARMS."
      },
      {
        "t": 441.01,
        "who": "mei",
        "text": "Mei: Remove & Substitute: cut 'very busy and nice'; swap 'ran quickly' for 'sprinted' and 'food' for 'char kway teow'."
      },
      {
        "t": 448.86,
        "who": "mei",
        "text": "Mei: Add & Move: add charcoal smoke and a short minor sentence — 'Nobody spoke.' — saving the strongest image for last!"
      },
      {
        "t": 456.99,
        "who": "adj",
        "text": "Addie: Okay... one single precise verb did look cooler than five 'verys'. Don't tell anyone."
      }
    ]
